 :lesson/sections
 [{:section/type :accuracy-pointer
   :section/id 7
   :section/title "Feminine words and exceptions"
   :section/body
   ["Have you ever noticed that many girls' names end in the letter \"a\"?"
    "For example Sandra, Linda, Fiona, Barbara, Maria, Elena, Sara, Victoria, Amanda etc."
    "Most Spanish words that end in \"a\" are feminine words. To say \"the\" with a feminine word you use la."
    "The house La casa The family La familia The party La fiesta The case La maleta The school La escuela There are some exceptions. Even though they end in \"a\", día and tequila are masculine words. To say \"the\" with masculine word you use el."
    "The day el día The tequila el tequila"]}]
