 :lesson/closing
 ["Congratulations you have finished step1 You have learned to effectively use a lot of Spanish. But have you noticed there is something missing?"
  "In the next 4 chapters you’ll multiply your Spanish considerably. Not just with new words, but with new simple-to-use new structures. You are about to get a lot more control of Spanish."
  "By the end of chapter 12 you will have many times more ability to express yourself in Spanish than you now have."
  "What’s missing?"
  "Well, you have been doing a lot of talking about yourself haven’t you? Its fine, you are very well prepared to take your Spanish to the next level."
  "Time to start using Spanish dialog. Time for questions and answers, making conversation and discussions, inquiries, and chat."
  "Good news."
  "With the foundation you have it will be easy."
  "Easy, but not a no brainer. You do have to apply yourself. Just keep doing what you are already doing and complete all the exercises, and by chapter 12 you’ll have a strong foundation for Spanish dialog."
  "See you in chapter 9. We’ll start to have a chat in Spanish."]}
